From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: never fetch device trees from lunch

When check_product fails, lunch runs vendor/lineage/build/tools/
roomservice.py, which reads LineageOS/mirror/main/default.xml from
GitHub and, for a matching device, writes a roomservice manifest and
syncs the tree. A build tree takes its device trees from its pinned
manifest, so a product that cannot be configured must stop lunch with
its own error instead: a product configuration mistake turned into a
network read and, on a match, a repository sync.

Replace that call with a message, and drop the dependency-only call of
the other branch: it only ever fetches the lineage.dependencies of a
device tree that is listed in a manifest, and a tree without one answers
"Trying dependencies-only mode on a non-existing device tree?" and does
nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 envsetup.sh | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/envsetup.sh b/envsetup.sh
index 453df75726ef0e74012b2818568a881bfea3d276..8d18618813d7e6ede609a308f9f6cc199a1ff644 100644
--- a/envsetup.sh
+++ b/envsetup.sh
@@ -596,16 +596,17 @@ function lunch()
 
     if ! check_product $product $release
     then
-        # if we can't find a product, try to grab it off the LineageOS GitHub
         T=$(gettop)
         cd $T > /dev/null
-        vendor/lineage/build/tools/roomservice.py $product
+        # A product that cannot be configured is a bug in its makefiles, not a
+        # device tree to download: nothing is fetched and no manifest is written.
+        echo "lunch: $product could not be configured; nothing is fetched" >&2
         cd - > /dev/null
         check_product $product $release
     else
         T=$(gettop)
         cd $T > /dev/null
-        vendor/lineage/build/tools/roomservice.py $product true
+        # The device trees come from the manifest; no dependency list is fetched.
         cd - > /dev/null
     fi
 
